<h1>✺ UV Reactive</h1>
<p class="lead">Under a black light some minerals glow in neon colours. Trace elements and defects in the crystal absorb invisible ultraviolet light and give it back as visible colour.</p>
<div class="uv-explain">
  <div><h3>Fluorescence</h3><p>A glow that lasts only while the UV light is on. Colours often differ between <strong>longwave</strong> (~365 nm, common LED flashlights), <strong>midwave</strong> (~310 nm) and <strong>shortwave</strong> (~254 nm) lamps.</p></div>
  <div><h3>Phosphorescence</h3><p>An afterglow that continues for a moment, or longer, after the lamp is switched off. Willemite and Franklin calcite are classic examples.</p></div>
  <div><h3>Tenebrescence</h3><p>A reversible colour change caused by light. Hackmanite and tugtupite deepen in colour after UV exposure and fade again.</p></div>
  <div><h3>Franklin &amp; Sterling Hill</h3><p>The zinc mines of Franklin and Sterling Hill in New Jersey are known as the "Fluorescent Mineral Capital of the World", famous for red calcite and green willemite. Franklinite, the ore mineral named after the town, does <em>not</em> fluoresce.</p></div>
</div>
<p class="uv-safety">⚠️ {{ site.uvSafety }} Reactions vary by locality, and many specimens of a "fluorescent" mineral don't glow at all.</p>
<input class="filter-input" type="search" placeholder="Filter {{ site.uvStones.length }} UV-reactive stones…" oninput="filterCards(this.value)">
<div class="grid uv-grid" id="cards">{% for c in site.uvStones %}
<a class="card uv-card" href="{{ c.url }}" style="--glow:{{ c.uv.glow }}">
  <div class="card-img uv-card-pair"><span class="h day">{% if c.uv.day %}<img loading="lazy" src="{{ c.uv.day.src | replace('width=480','width=240') }}" alt="{{ c.title }} in daylight">{% else %}<span class="gem-ph">☀</span>{% endif %}<i>☀ Daylight</i></span><span class="h uvl">{% if c.uv.uvImg %}<img loading="lazy" src="{{ c.uv.uvImg.thumbSrc or (c.uv.uvImg.src | replace('width=480','width=240')) }}" alt="{{ c.title }} under UV">{% else %}<span class="gem-ph">✺</span>{% endif %}<i>✺ Under UV</i></span></div>
  <div class="card-body"><strong>{{ c.title }}</strong>
    <span class="uv-waves">{% for w in c.uv.waves %}<i>{{ w }}</i>{% endfor %}</span>
    <span class="uv-line">{{ c.uv.lw or c.uv.sw or c.uv.mw }}</span>
  </div>
</a>{% endfor %}</div>
<p class="muted small">Photo credits: each stone page lists the photographer and license for its daylight and UV photos. Photos marked © Tiffany Stark are her own.</p>
<p class="muted small">Search tip: the <a href="/search/">search page</a> has a "UV reaction" filter (longwave, midwave, shortwave, phosphorescent, tenebrescent).</p>
<script>
function filterCards(q){q=q.toLowerCase();document.querySelectorAll('#cards .card').forEach(el=>{el.style.display=el.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(q)?'':'none'})}
</script>
